   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to moving the date of the\nmeeting of the electors and the method for the transmission of the\ncertificates of vote",
    "basePrintNo": "S8464",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8464-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§12-102, 12-104, 12-106 & 12-108, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8464\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to moving the date of the\nmeeting of the electors and the method for the transmission of the\ncertificates of vote\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend the date of the meeting of the electoral college.   \nSUMMARY OF\nPROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 12-104 of the election law, as amended by\nchapter 234 of the laws of 1976. Specifies that the electors of the\nElectoral College shall meet at a place decided by the secretary of\nstate on the first Tuesday after the second Wednesday in December.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAmending the date of the meeting of the electoral college ensures New\nYork compliance with the Electoral Count Reform Act.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
